<div id="2026-11-11-hermes-md-repair" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-11 — branch context file repaired (global rules restored, 3d domain re-seeded)</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> <code>.hermes.md</code> at the repo root and in the 3d worktree had both been replaced by a CSSNavigation branch overlay (70 lines, sections 1–7 missing, a pointer back to the very file it had overwritten). The root copy is restored from the last complete global version (commit 98eca4daa) — project overview, documentation system, hard rules, Director/Coder process — with a new section 8 that maps every branch to its port, host, sitename and owning domain. The 3d worktree keeps the same global body and carries its own section 8 for this branch only: print queue, printer LAN adapters, traveler, consignment counts, custom creation, NFS path rules and the schema boundary.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> A worktree is its own git root, so Hermes stops the context walk there and never reads the root file. Each worktree therefore has to repeat the global body and add one domain section. Committing a bare branch overlay at this path deleted the global rules for every checkout that merged it, and pointed the root file at itself. The stale copy also told this branch it lived on port 4012 with project #305, neither of which is true here (:4003, #272).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Rule now written down.</strong> Never replace the global body of this file with a branch overlay. Worktree copies repeat sections 1–7 verbatim, then add a section 8 headed "WORKER DOMAIN (this worktree only)". <code>Comserv/root/config/worktrees.json</code> remains the single owner of ports, hosts, sitenames and project ids.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Not done.</strong> The structural cause is unchanged: branch copies are still tracked at the same path, so merging a worktree branch up to main will bring that branch's section 8 with it. Moving per-branch domains to an untracked file is a separate decision.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>.hermes.md</code> (root and 3d worktree), <code>.hermes/docs-sync-state.json</code>.</p>
</div>
